Run football-league-app (Spring Server) first via .\gradlew bootRun
Then run football-league-client (CLI) second via .\gradlew.bat :app:run --console=plain (avoids gradle console interference)

EC2 VM needs:
export DB_URL='jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/football_league'
export DB_USERNAME='footballapp'
export DB_PASSWORD='PASSWORD'

Run EC2 Spring app via java -jar football-league-app-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar
CLI remains local via gradle (SOAP communicates with new AWS IP)